{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on request 17512f9f, for S8 (report f22ece9e). The family's\nsource may open on this ruling when identifiers (c+d) allows.\n\nItem 2, zero approvals: the first choice. The family's default Rules\ncompose the certified policy. A zero count needs `allowZeroApprovals:\ntrue`, each zero-approval extent needs its own opt-in, and every\napprover is `change.review`. This closes October 3.2 for the implicit\nform and the arbitrary approver. It does not close intentional zero\nreview, and the pages say so.\n\nOne condition on item 2. A person who creates a room alone must still\nland a first change by the user path. The whole-family witness includes\nthat path with the real commands: create a room, state the solo choice,\nland one change. The plan gives the count of commands today and in the\nnew family. If the new count is larger, say so before source opens, and\nI rule on where the first certified publish happens.\n\nItem 3, open founding: retain it and state it. `policy: \"open\"` admits\nany signer, and October 3.12 stays open by choice. The public Start\nregister needs it. S1 gives `found` its windows. Also take the narrower\nguard: the new Register refuses `open` with a nonempty `founders` list,\nbecause the pair misleads an operator. Do not report that guard as\nclosing 3.12. The witness is the one you name: another signer founds\nunder `open` and is refused under `keys`.\n\nItem 5, the default cohort: yes. The new default composes the certified\npolicy with its Native certificate and tree-verification consumers, the\nrequired-check union, and the protections of 68356c6c. A decoder import\nalone does not count.\n\nThe required-check union and the record of ruling 2.2 stand as you wrote\nthem.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}